    <item>
      <title>How to Choose a Dog-Friendly Ladder for Your Pontoon Boat</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/posts/first-post/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 21 Nov 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/posts/first-post/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Bringing your dog on the water adds fun, companionship, and memorable moments to any pontoon outing. Many boat owners prepare with life jackets, shaded rest areas, and plenty of clean water, although one item often overlooked is the ladder. A pontoon boat ladder plays a major role in helping dogs safely enter and exit the water, and the right design can make this experience easier for pets and people.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Dog-friendly features differ from the ones used for human-only boarding. Dogs rely on specific characteristics such as traction, stability, and shallow angles that help them climb confidently. This guide explains what sets a dog-friendly pontoon ladder apart, which features matter most, and why the Lippert SureStep™ ladder performs well for both dogs and human passengers.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      
